From 600f1c5c1225f7efa5cbf9e1831c7e6249e8b8a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:44:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2306/2312] media: uapi: mpeg2: document that D-pictures are
 optional

MPEG-1 D-pictures (DC coefficients only) are rare and not every MPEG-1
capable decoder decodes them: the Rockchip VDPU2 MPEG-1 mode has no
DC-only decoding and Hantro rejects the D picture coding type. Say so
in the uAPI, and that the rejection also applies to
VIDIOC_TRY_EXT_CTRLS, so that applications can find out whether a
decoder supports D-pictures before they hand one to it, and decode or
drop them otherwise.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 .../userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec-stateless.rst    | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec-stateless.rst b/Documentation/userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec-stateless.rst
index ecdd93072c8c..972b5b950b31 100644
--- a/Documentation/userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec-stateless.rst
+++ b/Documentation/userspace-api/media/v4l/ext-ctrls-codec-stateless.rst
@@ -1555,7 +1555,10 @@ FWHT Flags
       - Picture coding type for the frame covered by the current slice
 	(V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_I, V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_P,
 	V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_B, or V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_D in MPEG-1
-	sequences).
+	sequences). Decoding D-pictures is optional: drivers that cannot
+	decode them reject V4L2_MPEG2_PIC_CODING_TYPE_D, also in
+	``VIDIOC_TRY_EXT_CTRLS``, which applications can use to find out
+	whether D-pictures are supported.
     * - __u8
       - ``picture_structure``
       - Picture structure (1: interlaced top field, 2: interlaced bottom field,
